After a wrong answer, discard the candidate's whole rule, not merely its selected color or endpoint. Explicitly contrast its test prediction with all complete demonstrations, including unchanged lookalike cases, and change course only for an interpretation supported by that evidence. A depleted demo budget is not evidence that the remaining guess is correct. Keep output actions grounded in full demo replay rather than using repeated near-duplicate submissions to probe the grader.

